 "content": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.588), 20px);line-height:1.5\">Key indicators for Bangladesh&#8217;s development and humanitarian sector. Each figure shows its unit, period, geography and source.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Value</th><th>Period</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Children reached by new World Bank primary education programme</td><td>About 26 million</td><td>Approved 6 Nov 2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/world-bank-300-million-primary-education-bangladesh/\">World Bank, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>10-year-olds who cannot read a simple, age-appropriate text</td><td>About 50%</td><td>Latest World Bank estimate</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/world-bank-300-million-primary-education-bangladesh/\">World Bank, via The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Workers in the informal sector</td><td>About 84% (roughly 58 million people)</td><td>2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/05/world-bank-bangladesh-working-age-population-peaks-2045/\">World Bank, Demographic Change in South Asia</a></td></tr><tr><td>Year the working-age share of the population peaks</td><td>2045</td><td>Projection</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/05/world-bank-bangladesh-working-age-population-peaks-2045/\">World Bank, Demographic Change in South Asia</a></td></tr><tr><td>Garment minimum wage</td><td>Tk 12,500 a month (workers demand Tk 30,000)</td><td>Nov 2026; new scale due December</td><td><a href=\"/2026/11/07/garment-unrest-eases-workers-return-tension-ashulia/\">The Daily Star</a></td></tr><tr><td>Cost of the Health National Adaptation Plan</td><td>About US$1.4 billion (Tk 17,000 crore)</td><td>2026-2031</td><td><a href=\"/2026/10/29/climate-health-plan-needs-1-4-billion-over-five-years-study-finds/\">BRAC University C3ER study, Oct 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Secondary teachers with health education training</td><td>30.1% of those surveyed</td><td>2026</td><td><a href=\"/2026/10/29/only-30-of-secondary-teachers-trained-in-health-education-study-finds/\">DSHE school health study, with UNESCO</a></td></tr><tr><td>ADB loan for social protection reforms</td><td>US$250 million</td><td>Approved 24 Apr 2026</td><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/news/adb-approves-250-million-loan-implement-social-protection-reforms-bangladesh\">ADB</a></td></tr><tr><td>Widow allowance expansion under the ADB programme</td><td>At least 250,000 more women</td><td>Target</td><td><a href=\"https://www.adb.org/news/adb-approves-250-million-loan-implement-social-protection-reforms-bangladesh\">ADB</a></td></tr><tr><td>Internet users</td><td>82.8 million (47.0% of people)</td><td>Late 2025</td><td><a href=\"https://datareportal.com/reports/digital-2026-bangladesh\">DataReportal, Digital 2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>GDP growth projection</td><td>3.4%</td><td>FY26 and FY27</td><td>World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Non-performing loan ratio</td><td>33.2%</td><td>June 2026 (30.6% in Dec 2025)</td><td>World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, Oct 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Rohingya JRP appeal</td><td>USD 710.5 million</td><td>2026</td><td>Joint Response Plan 2026 update</td></tr><tr><td>Change in JRP appeal</td><td>26% lower than 2025</td><td>2026 vs 2025 (USD 934.5 million)</td><td>Oxfam, Aug 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Share of 2025 JRP appeal funded</td><td>46%</td><td>2025</td><td>Oxfam, citing OCHA</td></tr><tr><td>Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh</td><td>Nearly 1.2 million</td><td>2026</td><td>Oxfam</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-rohingya.png\"><img data-attachment-id=\"75\" data-permalink=\"/infographic-the-rohingya-appeal-is-shrinking/\" data-orig-file=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-rohingya.png\" data-orig-size=\"1600,900\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-title=\"Infographic: The Rohingya appeal is shrinking\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;Devlens Bangladesh. Sources: JRP 2026 update; Oxfam, citing OCHA.&lt;/p&gt;\n\" data-large-file=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-rohingya.png?w=1024\" src=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-rohingya.png\" alt=\"Bar chart: 2025 Rohingya appeal $934.5 million, of which about 46% was funded, and 2026 appeal $710.5 million, 26% smaller\" class=\"wp-image-75\" /></a><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Graphic: Devlens Bangladesh. Sources: JRP 2026 update; Oxfam, citing OCHA.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-economy.png\"><img data-attachment-id=\"76\" data-permalink=\"/infographic-bad-loans-are-still-rising/\" data-orig-file=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-economy.png\" data-orig-size=\"1600,900\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-title=\"Infographic: Bad loans are still rising\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;Devlens Bangladesh. Source: World Bank, Bangladesh Development Update, October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;\n\" data-large-file=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-economy.png?w=1024\" src=\"/media/2026/10/devlens-economy.png\" alt=\"Bar chart: non-performing loans rose from 30.6% in December 2025 to 33.2% in June 2026. GDP growth projected at 3.4% for FY26 and FY27\" class=\"wp-image-76\" /></a><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Graphic: Devlens Bangladesh. Source: World Bank, October 2026.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"color:#5b5b57;font-size:14px\">Last updated: 7 November 2026. See the linked articles for full sourcing: <a href=\"/2026/10/29/world-bank-projects-3-4-growth-for-bangladesh-and-calls-for-banking-energy-and-revenue-reforms/\">World Bank update</a>, <a href=\"/2026/10/29/rohingya-response-the-2026-appeal-is-a-quarter-smaller-and-still-underfunded/\">Rohingya response funding</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Coming next</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Interactive dashboards on poverty, climate and disaster risk, humanitarian funding, food security, WASH, education, health, gender, migration, social protection and localisation.</p>\n\n\n",
